Additionally, the regulatory section removes compliance conclusions and the GPT-4o retirement numbers are retained only with primary-source verification. The title now specifies the epistemic and ontological-calibration content.

The reader is asked to hold the paper to its own standard. Claims about internal states are underdetermined by outputs (P1); claims about received honesty are underdetermined by text (P2); scalar truthfulness is non-identifiable across heterogeneous dimensions (P3); calibration is necessary but not sufficient (P4, A1, A4, A5); and the architecture's core is epistemic, not metaphysical (P12).

