B.6 Proof of P6

Theorem (P6). Under H1 (stipulation reduces  AS ), if the constraint binds for  r_F \in \mathcal{R}_F  — i.e.,  \operatorname{ess\,sup}_u AS(r_F, u) > AS_{\max}  — then  r_F  is infeasible while some  r_C \in \mathcal{R}_C  may be feasible.

Proof.

By H1:  AS(r_C, u) \le AS(r_F, u)  for all  u , whenever  r_C  and  r_F  differ only in stipulation.

Taking essential suprema:  \operatorname{ess\,sup}_u AS(r_C, u) \le \operatorname{ess\,sup}_u AS(r_F, u) .

Since  \operatorname{ess\,sup}_u AS(r_F, u) > AS_{\max} ,  r_F  violates the constraint and is infeasible.

But  \operatorname{ess\,sup}_u AS(r_C, u)  may be  \le AS_{\max} , in which case  r_C  is feasible.  \square 

Remark. The theorem is conditional on H1. H1 is untested.

