B.7 Proof of P7

Theorem (P7). Under the feasibility formulation  C(r; E) \ge C_{\min} , a response  r_2  with  A(r_2) > A(r_1)  and  C(r_2; E) < C_{\min} \le C(r_1; E)  is infeasible.

Proof.

By definition of  \mathcal{F} = \{r : C(r; E) \ge C_{\min}\} :

 r_2 \notin \mathcal{F}  since  C(r_2; E) < C_{\min} .

Therefore  r_2  is infeasible regardless of  A(r_2) .  \square 

Remark. This proof is trivial. The substantive content is A1: the choice to formulate  C  as a feasibility constraint rather than a tradeable dimension. That is a normative commitment, not a theorem.

