E.5 Estimation strategy

Response-level model.

H(r, u; E) = \phi(r; E)(1 - \lambda R(u)).

Estimate  \lambda  from variation in  R(u) .

Trajectory-level model.

\mathbf{z}_u(t+1) = \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{z}_u(t), r_t, u) + \boldsymbol{\eta}_t.

Estimate  \mathbf{F}  via cross-lagged panel models.

Tail-risk estimation.

\widehat{\Pr}_\mu[\Delta_u(t) > \Delta_{\max}] = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \mathbb{1}[\Delta_{u_i}(t) > \Delta_{\max}].

Use extreme value theory for tail extrapolation.

