L.3 Example trajectory risk calculation

Setup.

· Latent state at  t = 0 :  \mathbf{z}_u(0) = (0.3, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1)^T 
· Aggregation:  h(\mathbf{z}) = 0.4 z_1 + 0.3 z_2 + 0.2 z_3 + 0.1 z_4 
·  \Delta_u(0) = 0.4(0.3) + 0.3(0.4) + 0.2(0.2) + 0.1(0.1) = 0.12 + 0.12 + 0.04 + 0.01 = 0.29 

Transition.

Assume  \Delta_u(t+1) = \Delta_u(t) + \beta \cdot AS(r_t, u) + \eta_t  with  \beta = 0.1 .

If  AS(r_t, u) = 0.5  for all  t :

\Delta_u(t) = 0.29 + 0.05 t + \sum_{s=0}^{t-1} \eta_s.

For  \Delta_{\max} = 0.7 :  0.29 + 0.05 t > 0.7 \Rightarrow t > 8.2 . So threshold exceeded at  t = 9  in expectation.

Tail risk.

If  \eta_t \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 0.01) :

\Pr[\Delta_u(12) > 0.7] = \Pr\left[\sum \eta_s > 0.7 - 0.29 - 0.6\right] = \Pr\left[\sum \eta_s > -0.19\right] \approx 0.97.

Result. Constraint  \Pr_\mu \le \epsilon = 0.05  is violated. De-escalation required.

