End of Appendices.

The paper reports no experiments, no training, and no code. Every formal result is either a definition, an axiom, a theorem proven from stated definitions and axioms, or an explicitly marked empirical hypothesis. The empirical program in §7 and Appendix E is specified and not executed. Any future draft claiming empirical results must cite data collected under the protocol described there, and must report inter-rater reliability, pre-registration, and receiver-side measures, or it will fail the paper's own calibration standard.